architecture governance-grammar
  canonical_name GovernanceGrammar
  family institutional
  domain Institutional / Governance as verbs a person already knows
  layer contract
  semantic_question What does a community see when it decides something, and what carries that decision underneath?
  purpose Fourteen governance verbs declared once -- Proposal, Decision, Vote, Discussion, Role, Delegation, Budget, FundingRequest, Milestone, Execution, Receipt, Policy, Member, Council -- with eight backings that may carry any of them, so the same rendered thing can be a database tally, a human approving, a Snapshot signal or a Safe threshold without the machinery reaching the page.
  maturity implemented
  node_types GovernanceVerb
  node_types GovernanceBacking
  node_types GovernanceRule
  edge_types carried_by
  edge_types bounded_by
  internal_calculus most governance in this estate is not blockchain governance. A PTA vote, a moderator appointment, a household spending decision and a community funding proposal need no wallet, and making them carry one would be the protocol leaking into the vocabulary
  internal_calculus human_approval is the first backing because it is the honest default: most decisions are made by a person who is allowed to make them
  internal_calculus a backing is chosen per verb, not per community, so a group can take its votes in a database and its treasury through a Safe without either fact reaching the page
  internal_calculus governance mostly declares the rules under which an action may execute without a vote; a vote is what happens when an act falls outside them. Proposing and voting on everything is overhead, not maturity
  invariant every verb states what it cannot be read to mean, because the failure here is always one shape: a record of an intention read as the thing having happened
  invariant only a backing that can settle may be offered where settlement is claimed, and the institution's declared world still gates it
  forbidden_inference a proposal -> a decision, or authority to act on it
  forbidden_inference a tally -> the membership's view; it is what was said by those who said it
  forbidden_inference a receipt reference -> settlement; it is a digest of something presented
  forbidden_inference a threshold reached on a Safe -> a transaction that landed; it is authority to submit
  source_path schemas/control/governance.cue
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tools/compile_governance.zig
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/generated/native_governance.h
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/main.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCMS/content-types/governance_proposal.json
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCMS/content-types/governance_vote.json
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCMS/content-types/governance_decision.json
  witness 2026-09-26 the package vets and exports: fourteen verbs and eight backings, three of which can settle and five of which cannot, each carrying its own refusal
  witness 2026-09-26 compiled from CUE into generated/native_governance.h by a Zig generator that refuses an unknown field, and served natively at /s/governance/grammar: 22 rows, fourteen verbs each printed with the sentence that bounds it and eight backings marked by whether they can settle
  witness 2026-09-26 the build asserts the count of settling backings, so a fourth cannot appear in the header without the check failing
  witness 2026-09-26 bound and exercised: 112 proposals and 9 decisions derived through the CMS organ from obligations the program fabric already held, and a member signed in and cast a real vote -- recorded as user:1, for, human_approval -- then changed it, which replaced the row rather than adding to the tally, because one person holds one position
  witness 2026-09-26 the three acts refuse before they record: an unauthenticated POST answers 401 saying an act carries the name of whoever performed it, a choice that is not for, against or abstain answers 400, and a request from another origin answers 403
  known_gap the rule form is declared and unused: no community has stated a ceiling, and nothing enforces one
